<title>USA: U.S. Lawmaker concerned by circuit-breaker plans.</title>
<headline>U.S. Lawmaker concerned by circuit-breaker plans.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Rep. Edward Markey, D-Mass., on Monday reiterated his his concerns about changing the current stock market circuit breakers.</p>
<p>In a letter to Securities and Exchange Commission Chairman Arthur Levitt, Markey noted that altering the circuit breakers at this time &quot;could contribute to a much higher level of market volatility,&quot; given its current high levels.</p>
<p>That, he said, might impair investor confidence &quot;or result in other unforseen consequences.&quot;</p>
